{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791561431,"nonce":"BhldiI+JAEMGD/nJEZR39leriYQ=","message":"Design findings, no code yet. blinc_text already has a process-wide registry (blinc_text::global_font_registry(), what blinc_app::register_font writes to) and it wraps a fontdb::Database. blinc_text and usvg 0.44 both use fontdb 0.22.0, so the types are shared: FaceInfo is Clone and Source::Binary holds an Arc, so registered faces can be pushed into usvg's database with push_face_info without copying font bytes. blinc_svg does not depend on blinc_text today (both depend only on blinc_core), so there is no cycle if it did. Constraints: the usvg database is built once in a OnceLock (rasterize.rs system_fonts), so faces registered after the first \u003ctext\u003e SVG would be missed; it needs a generation counter on the registry and a rebuild when it changes. Only Binary-source faces need merging, system faces are already loaded there. The alternative that avoids a new crate edge is a provider hook in blinc_svg that blinc_app installs, which keeps embedders without blinc_text unaffected. Not started: paused for the architecture work.","files":null}]}